    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** serving as our clear offensive anchors. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an 87.03 score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a and the high-leverage utility of the #3 spot; his dynamic platoon edge against the righty makes him an absolute must-start. **James Wood** follows closely at 78.41, benefiting from the day\u2019s most exploitable matchup against Spence (6.03 xERA). His leadoff role combined with an elite 0.403 xwOBA positions him to be the primary engine for our Runs and SB categories today. Elsewhere, **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Gabriel Moreno** provide strong secondary support, with **Tyler Soderstrom** specifically benefiting from a notable park factor boost that pushes his score to 69.84, making him our most reliable corner infield option.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remainder of the lineup was tight, particularly regarding the fringe options. **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Kyle Karros** all occupy the \"Marginal\" bucket between 47 and 55, forced into the lineup to preserve our precious game caps despite suboptimal spots in the batting order. The most difficult bench decision involved **Henry Bolte** (47.80), who narrowly missed the cut behind the platoon-heavy profiles of our starters. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from park factors, his spot in the #8 hole against Jones rendered him the odd man out in favor of the higher-upside profiles like **Seiya Suzuki**, who earns a 62.65 score due to his high-leverage cleanup assignment against Lorenzen. We continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us without the depth of **Josh Naylor** or the speed-based utility of **Jose Caballero** for today\u2019s matchups. We are keeping a close eye on the late-afternoon weather reports, though no specific warnings currently threaten the viability of our starters.",
